{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\chuanle song\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content -Raw 'pipeline/reviews/motivation_review_20260926-210900.md'; Get-Content -Raw 'pipeline/designs/exp_design_20260926-210900.md'; Get-Content -Raw 'pipeline/reports/summary_20260926-211500.md'\"","aggregated_output":"# Motivation Review - AdaRES_project\n\n2026-09-26 21:09 Asia/Shanghai\n\n## 1. Goal\nAdaRES: improve a faithful standard-indicator 3D referring expression segmentation baseline by learning query confidence from metric-aligned evidence, targeting ScanRefer mIoU >= 0.515. B1 0.5020; B4-E30 0.5094; gap 0.0056. Goal constraints and bans checked: only server-2 GPUs 0/1, one independent task per GPU, released SPFormer sparse-UNet backbone/project decoder, fixed B2/B4 continuation, report mIoU/Acc@0.25/Acc@0.5/active queries/latency/peak memory, no validation tuning or banned server/checkpoint/weight scans.\n\n## 2. Story Status\n| Hypothesis | Status | Evidence | Gap |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Query competition confidence | Partial | B4-E30 0.5094 | Below Phase 1 target |\n| Metric-IoU targets | Negative | G1 0.4980 | No weight/label scan |\n| Token attention concentration | Weak/non-specific | Q1 oracle higher 260/388 train errors, concentration-only 0.08395 | Target-token control only 206/388 vs rotated 160/388 |\n| Scene attention support | Negative | Q2 oracle higher 70/388 | Opposite confidence direction |\n\n## 3. Experiment Assessment\nB1 0.5020, B4-E30 0.5094, D1 0.5080, F4 0.5060, H5 0.5061, G1 0.4980. Q1/Q2 are diagnostic inference probes, not trained results. Earlier J1 pooled text-mask contrast and P1 topology failed their specific directions.\n\n## 4. Gap Analysis\nThe 64-scene training cohort has selected mIoU 0.82256 and many missed high-IoU candidates. Neither raw token-attention concentration nor attention-mask agreement identifies the missed candidate with adequate specificity. Active queries and historical full-run latency/peak memory remain unmeasured.\n\n## 5. Design Rationale\nQ1 tested a token-level information path that B4 computes but does not explicitly pass to its confidence head; Q2 tested a distinct query-to-scene interaction. Their paired controls rule out admitting these mechanisms on present evidence. A future candidate needs a new inference-available, metric-aligned mechanism with frozen native paired controls and six hard gates.\n\n## 6. Next Batch\nNo admission. See `pipeline/designs/exp_design_20260926-210900.md`.\n\r\n# Experiment Design - AdaRES_project\n\n2026-09-26 21:09 Asia/Shanghai\n\n## 1. Motivation\nGoal: \"AdaRES: improve a faithful standard-indicator 3D referring expression segmentation baseline by learning query confidence from metric-aligned evidence, targeting ScanRefer mIoU >= 0.515.\" Active 0/2, candidate budget 2. Q1/Q2 tested whether already-computed attention paths could supply missing metric-aligned confidence.\n\n## 2. Current Best Results\n| ID | State | mIoU | Acc@0.25 | Acc@0.5 | spmIoU |\n|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| B1 | complete | 0.5020 | 0.610 | 0.553 | 0.467 |\n| B4-E30 | champion | 0.5094 | 0.608 | 0.562 | 0.474 |\n| H5 | early stop | 0.5061 | unavailable | unavailable | unavailable |\n| G1 | complete | 0.4980 | unavailable | unavailable | unavailable |\n\n## 3. Analysis & Direction\nQ1 showed oracle concentration 260/388 material training errors, but target-token mass only 206/388 versus rotated-token null 160/388, and concentration-only mIoU 0.08395 versus B4 0.82256. Q2 oracle scene-attention support exceeded selected in only 70/388, against its predeclared direction. See paired analysis and raw readouts.\n\n## 4. Experiment Plan\nReject Q1 attention-concentration confidence and Q2 attention-mask agreement at diagnosis/controls. No training candidate, model/config implementation, admission receipt, or validation tuning. A new independent route must be justified by native paired evidence and then pass backward, resource, independence and goal gates.\n\n## 5. GPU Allocation Plan\nServer-2 GPU0/1 were both idle at the targeted pre-probe query (0%, 1 MiB each). GPU0 inference probes completed. Both project queue slots remain vacant; no current post-probe occupancy claim. Server-6 excluded.\n\n## 6. Implementation Checklist\n- [x] Fixed 64 training-scene Q1/Q2 native readouts with repeated-forward controls.\n- [x] Q1 training annotation rotated-token null; Q2 previous-mask control.\n- [x] Raw outputs, code and hashes retained; diagnosis/controls assessed.\n- [ ] No backward/resource qualification, independent model package, receipt, sync, queue or training launch without a supported mechanism.\n\n## 7. Risk Assessment\nTraining subset is diagnostic, not generalization evidence. Q1 strict floating-point repeat deviations and Q2 one discrete repeat mismatch limit certainty. Attention weights may not be calibrated relevance estimates. Training annotation maps are not inference-available.\n\n## 8. Smell Check\nAttention entropy/temperature, token subset, support threshold, or fusion-weight sweeps would be tuning-only. A simple attention statistic added as a scalar to confidence is not a new justified information path. Neither route passes the three structural and causal standards.\n\nStatus: NO ADMISSION. Bounded Q1/Q2 executable routes exhausted this cycle; no global scientific exhaustion claim.\n\r\n================================================================================\n  Research Pipeline Report - AdaRES_project\n  2026-09-26 21:15 Asia/Shanghai (design tick)\n================================================================================\n\n## 0. Goal Status\n| Target | Champion | Gap | Phase |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| ScanRefer mIoU >= 0.5150 | AdaRES-B4-E30 0.5094 | 0.0056 | Phase 1 unmet; Phase 2 pending |\n\nB1 baseline 0.5020; champion gain +0.0074. Prepared monitor/goal preflight succeeded once and was not rerun.\n\n## 1. GPU Overview\n| Server | GPU | Util | Memory Used | Assignment |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---|\n| server-2 | 0 | 0% before probes | 1 MiB before probes | no project task; Q1/Q2 probes completed |\n| server-2 | 1 | 0% before probes | 1 MiB before probes | no project task |\n\nNo current occupancy conclusion follows from the pre-probe reading. Server-6 excluded.\n\n## 2. Running Experiments\n| ID | Config | Server | GPU | Epoch | Best mIoU | Acc@50 | spmIoU | No-Impr | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| - | - | - | - | - | - | - | - | - | none |\n\n## 3. Queue Status\n| Position | ID | Config | Status | Depends On | Server |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| - | - | - | no waiting or claiming tasks | - | - |\n\nActive 0/2 target; candidate budget 2. Q1/Q2 did not pass diagnosis/controls gates. No due research candidates.\n\n## 4. This Tick's Actions\n- Q1 fixed 64 training-scene token-attention diagnosis: 1660 expressions, 388 material errors. Oracle concentration higher in 260; standalone mIoU 0.08395 versus B4 0.82256; annotated-token mass higher in 206 versus rotated-token null 160. Repeated-forward strict numerical mismatch 2, max 8.67e-5.\n- Q2 independent query-to-scene attention support diagnosis: oracle higher in 70/388 final-mask comparisons and 25/388 prior-mask comparisons, opposite the predeclared direction. One repeated-forward discrete mismatch.\n- Preserved native read-only probe code, paired raw outputs, hashed analysis/review/design and research ledger. Inference peak reserved memory 3.48/3.56 GiB is not training peak. No native backward, implementation, receipt, sync, dispatch or queue mutation.\n- No pending questions in prepared snapshot. Resume only on a distinct inference-available confidence mechanism with frozen paired native controls and all six gates; bounded Q1/Q2 exhaustion is not global scientific exhaustion.\n\n## 5. Decisions Made\n- 2026-09-26 21:13 `route_change`: reject Q1/Q2, leave server-2 GPU0/1 unque