{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\chuanle song\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content -Raw 'pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-N1-N3_diagnosis_20260926-183100.md'; Get-Content -TotalCount 230 'AdaRES/tools/diagnose_adares_n3_collisions.py'; Get-Content -TotalCount 220 'AdaRES/tools/diagnose_adares_o2_appearance_counterfactual.py'\"","aggregated_output":"# Native diagnostic cycle: N1, N2, N3\n\n2026-09-26 18:31 Asia/Shanghai. No training admission or queue mutation.\n\n## N1: Mask/indicator gradient interference\nAt B4-E30 best checkpoint, native training batches [0,1], [256,257], [64,65], [128,129] gave indicator-versus-mask gradient cosines on `dec.x_mask.0.weight` of -0.868, -0.079, +0.194 and -0.194. Corresponding unweighted indicator/mask gradient norm ratios were 0.251, 0.773, 0.822 and 1.420. The initialized B4 batches [0,1] and [256,257] had -0.982 and -0.997 cosines but indicator gradient norms below 1% of mask norm. G1 initialized batch [0,1] also had -0.987. On trained B4, detached mask evidence preserved forward losses and zeroed the indicator gradient into mask projection. A fixed, RNG-restored, single-parameter SGD step on [0,1] changed mask loss by +0.00008852 with live evidence versus +0.00008772 with detach, a roughly 0.00000080 difference. This is a controlled path test, not a full optimizer step or a training efficacy estimate. Gradient signs are mixed across trained batches. Reject detach-only as an ablation; no supported independent confidence mechanism or admission.\n\n## N2: Same-referent expression consistency\nIn the fixed 16 validation scenes, 135 object groups supplied 323 same-object expression pairs. The selected masks disagreed (IoU <0.5) for 146 of 316 pairs with consistent oracle masks (IoU >=0.5); 76 discordant pairs had one selected IoU <0.25 and the other >=0.5. But the label-free nearest-language proxy grouped the same object in only 121/441 expressions (27.4%). Mask overlap alone identified the same object in 171/354 overlapping scene pairs (48.3%). Both proxy measurements are observational and derived from a fixed validation subset. Reject these grouping rules; no validation cutoff search or oracle-object-ID use at inference.\n\n## N3: Distinct-target selection collisions\nNative training batches contained 44 distinct-target expression pairs in eight scenes. Trained B4 produced two selected-mask collisions (mask IoU >=0.5). The same fixed criterion over 64 training scenes found only 6 collisions in 365 distinct-target pairs (1.6%). One collision scene accounted for three pairs; individual confidence readouts remained high. A collision-only loss would have sparse exposure in the native batch protocol, and the current screen does not establish a general performance bottleneck. Reject this specific exclusivity mechanism, not all cross-expression reasoning.\n\n## Limitations and route decision\nThese are bounded native screens, not a broad literature novelty review or proof that no future route exists. The G1 and B4 checkpoints are not a fresh matched training-seed control. No candidate was admitted: N1 lacks a non-ablation mechanism, N2 lacks reliable label-free grouping, and N3 has sparse qualifying pairs. The next cycle should start from a predeclared, independently motivated confidence mechanism with a native matched intervention; do not rename or tune these three failures.\n\r\nimport argparse\r\nimport json\r\nimport sys\r\nfrom pathlib import Path\r\n\r\nimport gorilla\r\nimport torch\r\nimport torch.nn.functional as F\r\n\r\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\r\nsys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT))\r\n\r\nfrom ipdn.dataset import build_dataset\r\nfrom ipdn.model_paper5.adares_b4_query_competition import IPDN\r\nfrom ipdn.utils import get_root_logger\r\n\r\n\r\ndef main():\r\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\r\n    parser.add_argument(\"config\")\r\n    parser.add_argument(\"checkpoint\")\r\n    parser.add_argument(\"--indices\", type=int, nargs=\"+\", default=(0, 1, 64, 65, 128, 129, 256, 257))\r\n    parser.add_argument(\"--gpu-id\", type=int, default=1)\r\n    parser.add_argument(\"--output\", required=True)\r\n    args = parser.parse_args()\r\n    gorilla.set_cuda_visible_devices([args.gpu_id], 1)\r\n    gorilla.set_random_seed(1999)\r\n    cfg = gorilla.Config.fromfile(args.config)\r\n    dataset = build_dataset(cfg.data.train, get_root_logger())\r\n    model = IPDN(**cfg.model).cuda()\r\n    checkpoint = torch.load(args.checkpoint, map_location=\"cpu\")\r\n    loaded = model.load_state_dict(checkpoint.get(\"model\", checkpoint), strict=False)\r\n    allowed = {\"text_encoder.embeddings.position_ids\", \"text_encoder.embeddings.token_type_ids\"}\r\n    if loaded.missing_keys or set(loaded.unexpected_keys) - allowed:\r\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"Checkpoint mismatch: {loaded}\")\r\n    model.eval()\r\n    capture = {}\r\n\r\n    def capture_decoder(module, inputs, output):\r\n        capture[\"output\"] = output\r\n\r\n    model.dec.register_forward_hook(capture_decoder)\r\n    pairs = []\r\n    for scene in args.indices:\r\n        batch = dataset.collate_fn([dataset[scene]])\r\n        with torch.no_grad():\r\n            model(batch, mode=\"loss\")\r\n            output = capture[\"output\"]\r\n            masks = output[\"masks\"].sigmoid().gt(0.5)\r\n            confidence = F.softmax(output[\"indis\"], dim=-1)[..., 1]\r\n            selected = confidence.argmax(-1)\r\n            targets = batch[\"gt_spmasks\"]\r\n            ids = batch[\"object_idss\"]\r\n            for left in range(len(ids)):\r\n                for right in range(left + 1, len(ids)):\r\n                    if len(ids[left]) != 1 or len(ids[right]) != 1 or ids[left] == ids[right]:\r\n                        continue\r\n                    a = masks[left, selected[left]]\r\n                    b = masks[right, selected[right]]\r\n                    valid = ~(output[\"batch_mask\"][left] | output[\"batch_mask\"][right])\r\n                    overlap = ((a & b) & valid).sum().float() / (((a | b) & valid).sum().clamp_min(1))\r\n                    def quality(expr, pred):\r\n                        target = targets[expr].to(pred.device).gt(0.5)\r\n                        pred = pred[:target.numel()]\r\n                        return float((pred & target).sum().float() / (pred | target).sum().clamp_min(1))\r\n                    pairs.append({\r\n                        \"scene\": scene,\r\n                        \"left\": left,\r\n                        \"right\": right,\r\n                        \"overlap\": float(overlap),\r\n                        \"left_iou\": quality(left, a),\r\n                        \"right_iou\": quality(right, b),\r\n                        \"left_confidence\": float(confidence[left, selected[left]]),\r\n                        \"right_confidence\": float(confidence[right, selected[right]]),\r\n                    })\r\n        capture.clear()\r\n    result = {\"scenes\": len(args.indices), \"distinct_target_pairs\": len(pairs), \"pairs\": pairs}\r\n    Path(args.output).write_text(json.dumps(result, indent=2), encoding=\"utf-8\")\r\n    print(json.dumps({\"scenes\": result[\"scenes\"], \"distinct_target_pairs\": len(pairs),\r\n                      \"overlap_ge_half\": sum(row[\"overlap\"] >= 0.5 for row in pairs)}))\r\n\r\n\r\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\r\n    main()\r\nimport argparse\r\nimport json\r\nimport statistics\r\nimport sys\r\nimport types\r\nfrom pathlib import Path\r\n\r\nimport gorilla\r\nimport torch\r\nimport torch.nn.functional as F\r\n\r\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\r\nsys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT))\r\n\r\nfrom ipdn.dataset import build_dataset\r\nfrom ipdn.model_paper5.adares_b4_query_competition import IPDN\r\nfrom ipdn.utils import get_root_logger\r\n\r\n\r\ndef predictor(self, scan_ids, object_idss, ann_ids, out, superpoints,\r\n              gt_pmasks, gt_spmasks, fps_seed_sp):\r\n    rows = []\r\n    for index, truth in enumerate(gt_pmasks):\r\n        masks = out[\"masks\"][index].sigmoid().gt(0.5)[:, superpoints]\r\n        target = truth.gt(0.5).to(masks.device)\r\n        ious = (masks & target).sum(-1).float() / (\r\n            (masks | target).sum(-1).clamp_min(1).float()\r\n        )\r\n        confidence = F.softmax(out[\"indis\"][index], dim=-1)[:, 1]\r\n        selected = int(confidence.argmax())\r\n        rows.append({\r\n            \"selected\": selected,\r\n            \"iou\": float(ious[selected]),\r\n            \"oracle_iou\": float(ious.max()),\r\n            \"mask\": torch.where(masks[selected])[0].tolist(),\r\n            \"confidence\": float(confidence[selected]),\r\n        })\r\n    return {\"rows\": rows}\r\n\r\n\r\ndef main():\r\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\r\n    parser.add_argument(\"config\")\r\n    parser.add_argument(\"checkpoint\")\r\n    parser.add_argument(\"--output\", required=True)\r\n    parser.add_argument(\"--scenes\", type=int, default=16)\r\n    parser.add_argument(\"--gpu-id\", type=int, default=0)\r\n    parser.add_argument(\"--split\", choices=(\"train\", \"val\"), default=\"train\")\r\n    args = parser.parse_args()\r\n    gorilla.set_cuda_visible_devices([args.gpu_id], 1)\r\n    gorilla.set_random_seed(1999)\r\n    cfg = gorilla.Config.fromfile(args.config)\r\n    data_cfg = getattr(cfg.data, args.split).copy()\r\n    data_cfg.training = False\r\n    data_cfg.aug = False\r\n    data_cfg.with_elastic = False\r\n    data_cfg.lang_num_max = 32\r\n    dataset = build_dataset(data_cfg, get_root_logger())\r\n    model = IPDN(**cfg.model).cuda()\r\n    model.eval()\r\n    checkpoint = torch.load(args.checkpoint, map_location=\"cpu\")\r\n    loaded = model.load_state_dict(checkpoint.get(\"model\", checkpoint), strict=False)\r\n    allowed = {\"text_encoder.embeddings.position_ids\",\r\n               \"text_encoder.embeddings.token_type_ids\"}\r\n    if